This is going to be a very basic trick, nevertheless at my level of
expertise I was proud to think of it and pulling it off brought me a
lot of satisfaction.

I am playing my Nethack on a very old computer at home that does not
have internet access.  I'm using Hearse and a thumb drive to get bones
files.  My current character loaded one in the 2nd level of the Mines,
and it was obviously a low-level wizard: killed by pony, ornamental
cope, 2 spellbooks, some rings and potions.  One of the items in the
pile that did not curse was a blessed scroll that I later price-ID'd
at 80.

Since this was either enchant armor or remove curse, I picked up all
cursed items in this pile and my stash, took off all armor, put on the
cursed CoMR, and then read the blessed scroll.  If it was enchant
armor, my cloak would become blessed.  If it was remove curse, the
bones items would all be uncursed.  Either way, I was going to get a
non-cursed CoMR out of it.  As it turned out, it was remove curse, and
so a lot of useful tools and wands became available to me.

Intentionally putting on a known cursed item was the new wrinkle for
me.  I was able to do this becasue I knew exactly what the effects of
the scrolls were when blessed.


